<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nadol</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Naddula</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nadol, the medieval Naddula, is a town in Pali district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Around 950 Lakshmana, a member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chauhan">Chahamanas</a> of Shakambhari, founded a kingdom there that ruled southern Marwar until the early 13th century, usually as feudatories of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaulukya-dynasty">Chaulukyas of Gujarat</a>. The town is known for its medieval Jain temples.</p></div>
